{"OptimizedCursorPaginator permits negative cursor offsets and uses them for queryset slicing, while other paginators treat negative offsets as invalid. Since Cursor.from_string accepts arbitrary offsets, this enables unvalidated negative offsets to reach query execution and produce inconsistent behavior or errors.": 0.9436849355697632, "OptimizedCursorPaginator applies math.floor/ceil to the ordered field value and returns raw cursor.value, but the audit logs endpoint orders by a datetime field (\"-datetime\"). This will raise type errors or build invalid queryset filters, breaking the endpoint when optimized pagination is enabled.": 0.9337590336799622, "The endpoint gates optimized pagination using request.user.is_superuser, but the permission class grants access based on is_active_superuser(request). Active superusers without org membership can pass permission checks yet hit an AttributeError when organization_context.member is None.": 0.9019345045089722}